---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const updated = "2 October 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Terms — PaceStreak"
  description="The terms for using PaceStreak: accounts, acceptable use, your content, health and safety, moderation, and ending your account."
  path="/terms"
>
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-20">
    <div class="wrap max-w-2xl">
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[0.92rem] text-dim">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <div class="prose-page mt-10">
        <p>
          These terms cover the PaceStreak websites and the app at
          app.pacestreak.com. PaceStreak is a free, open-source project run by
          its maintainer ("we" below); it has no paid plans and no
          advertising. These terms are written to be read. By creating an
          account you agree to them and to the{" "}
          <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Not medical advice</h2>
        <p>
          PaceStreak tracks consistency. It is not a coach, a doctor or a
          physiotherapist, and nothing in it is medical advice. Check with a
          professional before starting or changing a training programme,
          especially if you have an injury or a health condition.{" "}
          <strong>Stop if something hurts.</strong> The app is built so that
          resting never costs you your streak: use a rest day, a freeze or a
          pause.
        </p>
        <p>
          The built-in training plans, progression hints and interval timers
          are general suggestions for healthy adults, not a programme made for
          you. Skip, change or stop any session that doesn't suit you.
        </p>
        <p>
          The same goes for everything else the app works out for you:
          nutrition targets, the energy-burn estimate, insights, coach cards
          and readiness scores are estimates from what you logged, not a
          diagnosis or a diet plan. Food data looked up by barcode comes from
          Open Food Facts, a volunteer database; check it against the label.
          If you have, or are recovering from, an eating disorder, talk to a
          professional before tracking food or weight.
        </p>
        <p>
          Habits you're breaking, such as smoking or drinking, are tracked to
          help you notice and count clean days. PaceStreak is not a treatment
          programme. If you're struggling, contact a doctor or a local support
          service, and in an emergency call your local emergency number.
        </p>

        <h2>Your account</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>You must be 13 or older. Under 16, your account is private-only.</li>
          <li>Use a real email address you control, and keep your password to yourself. Turning on two-factor authentication is a good idea.</li>
          <li>One person per account. Official PaceStreak accounts carry a verified mark; don't pretend to be us or anyone else.</li>
          <li>You're responsible for what happens under your account. Tell us straight away if you think someone else has access.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Your content</h2>
        <p>
          Your habits, training log, notes, photos, comments and everything
          else you put in stay yours. You give PaceStreak permission to store, process and
          display them only as needed to run the service, and only to the
          people your settings allow. You can export everything, and deleting
          your account deletes it (see the privacy policy for timings).
        </p>

        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>Don't use PaceStreak to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>harass, threaten, shame or impersonate anyone, including through comments, handles or display names;</li>
          <li>post anything illegal, sexual, hateful, or that promotes self-harm or disordered eating;</li>
          <li>upload content you don't have the right to share, or anything showing another person without their permission;</li>
          <li>log fake sessions or implausible numbers to game challenges or leaderboards;</li>
          <li>scrape, overload or attack the service, or get around its limits, privacy rules or blocks;</li>
          <li>access anyone else's account or data.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If you find a security problem, report it privately to{" "}
          <a href="mailto:hello@pacestreak.com">hello@pacestreak.com</a>. We
          won't pursue good-faith research that respects these terms and other
          people's data.
        </p>

        <h2>Moderation</h2>
        <p>
          Anyone can report a person, comment, event, group or challenge. A
          person reviews every report. We may remove content, remove someone
          from leaderboards, or suspend their social features.
          A suspension never touches your own training log: you can still log,
          see your history and export it. We may close accounts used for
          serious or repeated abuse. Every moderation action is recorded.
        </p>

        <h2>The service</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            We work to keep PaceStreak running. Availability is public at{" "}
            <a href="https://status.pacestreak.com">status.pacestreak.com</a>.
            But the service is provided as is, and we can't promise it will
            always be available or free of errors.
          </li>
          <li>Features will change. We'll give notice in the app before removing something you rely on, and your data can always be exported first.</li>
          <li>
            The code is licensed{" "}
            <a href="https://github.com/PaceStreak">AGPL-3.0</a> (the status
            page and organization files are MIT). You're welcome to run your
            own copy under that licence. The licence covers the code, not the
            PaceStreak name, logo or wordmark, so a modified copy you run for
            others needs its own name.
          </li>
          <li>
            Barcode food data is &copy; Open Food Facts contributors, available
            under the{" "}
            <a href="https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/">Open Database Licence</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            If the project ever has to shut down, we'll give account holders at
            least 30 days' notice in the app and by email, so everyone can
            export their data first.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Liability</h2>
        <p>
          PaceStreak is provided free of charge. To the extent the law allows,
          we aren't liable for indirect or consequential losses, for lost
          data beyond what we can restore, or for injuries or health effects
          from training, eating or anything else you choose to do, which are
          your decisions. Nothing here limits liability that can't be limited
          by law, or your rights as a consumer where you live.
        </p>

        <h2>Ending it</h2>
        <p>
          You can delete your account at any time from Settings → Data. It is
          removed after a 30-day grace period, and signing in during that time
          cancels the deletion. If we close an account for abuse, we'll say
          why, and you can still ask for an export of your training data.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          This page is versioned publicly. If a change matters, we'll tell
          account holders in the app before it takes effect. Carrying on using
          PaceStreak after that means you accept the new terms; if you don't,
          you can export your data and delete your account.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="mailto:hello@pacestreak.com">hello@pacestreak.com</a>, read
          by a person.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
